 "plaques": [
  {
   "at": [
    -19.4,
    2.4,
    2.2
   ],
   "rot": 135,
   "text": "THE OSSUARY UNDERCROFT\n\nSix hundred brothers, six thousand candles, one shovel.\n\nThe Sexton squared every corner himself. Walk soft: below the Cloister and the Basilica alike, the kingdom keeps its bones in one basket."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    11.4,
    0,
    11.2
   ],
   "rot": -160,
   "text": "THE WATCHERS\n\nThe dead face east, toward the morning that is owed them.\n\nTurn them right and the reliquary opens its teeth. Turn them wrong and they will simply go on being patient."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    4.2,
    0,
    -1.4
   ],
   "rot": 160,
   "text": "THE BELL-OX'S STALL\n\nBourdon hauled the great bells up the tower road, yoke and harness, sixty years.\n\nWhen the carting ended they stabled him down here with the bell that cracked. He would not leave it. He has not left it."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    -5.6,
    0,
    -8.8
   ],
   "rot": 25,
   "text": "Above this stair the dead kept birds.\n\nThe sisters swore the singing reached even here, on good mornings, threading down the tower like light through a well."
  }
 ],
